# The heat equation
# u_t = D u_xx on a rod of length 1 whose ends are kept at zero, solved on
# 49 inner points (the method of lines). A hot spot spreads and fades; the
# smoothest shape, sin(pi x), decays as exp(-pi^2 D t).
par D=1,n=50
u0=0
u50=0
u[1..49]'=D*n^2*(u[j+1]-2*u[j]+u[j-1])
init u[20..30]=1
@ total=0.2,dt=0.00005,meth=rungekutta,nout=40
@ xp=t,yp=u25,xlo=0,xhi=0.2,ylo=0,yhi=1
done
